# HTTPS for Retake with Caddy (https://caddyserver.com), on the same machine as `docker compose up`. Caddy gets and
# renews the certificate on its own. Change the hostname to yours: it must match RETAKE_PUBLIC_URL in deploy/.env.
#
#   caddy run --config deploy/Caddyfile        (or copy the block into /etc/caddy/Caddyfile)
#
# What Retake needs from any proxy, which Caddy does by default:
#   - the live updates (/api/events and /p/<project>/api/events, server-sent events) passed through unbuffered;
#   - responses that take 30 seconds or more: video relayed from your computer, agents waiting for notes;
#   - request bodies of any size (retake push --remote sends 8 MiB pieces).
# With nginx that is `proxy_buffering off; proxy_read_timeout 120s; client_max_body_size 0;`.
#
# Seen from inside the container, Caddy is the docker bridge, so also set RETAKE_TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.16.0.0/12 in
# deploy/.env: then failed sign-in links and tokens are counted per visitor, not per proxy.

review.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}
